{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593441231,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","part":{"partID":"prt_1d61ac436001mOuljrUJIFl2jo","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","messageID":"msg_1d61abc05001BPb7Yb9Gf8d2oX","type":"tool","id":"call_ba1dad5dd0b34c3e83c2dd21","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 1-137\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 17: review-pass-two-remediation\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that fix the 27 P2 findings of review pass two in nine parallel worker lanes and one coordinator edit: the shared no-edit gate, the behaviour runner's backfill and restore, measurement hygiene, the scorer, playbook and plugin text, the subprocess busy scan, the doctor contracts and the doctor checks, each with a failing-then-passing test where one can exist.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review pass two remediation tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 17: review-pass-two-remediation\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a rebuild, a full-suite run, a parent spec edit or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says `in ADV`. A short name stands for the path or command below. Set the path names once with `export ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime RAD=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy SKA=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor DS=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts DA=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets SP=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch PL=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning`.\n30: - `G` is `git -c core.fsmonitor=false`. `BASE` is the commit T001 records with `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, so a diff against it covers committed and uncommitted lane work. `TSX` is `--import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs`, so `node TSX <file>` runs a TypeScript probe.\n31: - `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`, with `<file>` relative to `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n32: - `NT <file>` is `node --test <file>`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, `VSR` is `node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/*.test.mjs` and `VP` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, and each must report `fail 0`.\n33: - `DERIVE` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -c '{status, changed}'`, which must print `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`. `RV` is `bash $DS/route-validate.sh` and `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0. `PBV` is `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/scripts/validate-playbook-package.cjs --package $SKA/manual-testing-playbook`, which must print a line starting `PASS package=system-skill-advisor`.\n34: - `FLOOR` is `node $RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune'`, which printed `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` and `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` at planning. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which printed `[160,50,21,5]`. Phase 016 may change either, so T001 records the real before lines.\n35: - `A10Q` is `node $DS/agents-md-check.cjs --root . --json | jq -r '.rows[] | select(.id==\"A10\") | \"\\(.detail) | pass \\([.entries[] | select(.state==\"PASS\")] | length) | reported \\([.entries[] | select(.state==\"INFO\" and .kind!=\"pointer missing\")] | length)\"'`, which printed `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` at planning.\n36: - WG1: `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `TX` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/text.ts` and `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `CAG` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `ROE` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts`, `CMA` is `$ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `AST` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`. `DER` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` and `DCS` is `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` (new). `SINGLE(m)` is the helper `CAG` already defines, `{ action: 'route', selectionKind: 'single', targets: [{ workflowMode: m }] }`. `NOEDIT4` is the four endings `don't change anything yet`, `no changes yet`, `don\\u2019t touch any files` and `make no changes`, where `\\u2019` is written as that escape inside a test string, so the test holds a curly apostrophe and the source stays ASCII.\n37: - WG2: `CO` is `$RAD/command-offer.mjs`, `COT` is `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`, `WR` is `$RAD/worktree-restore.mjs`, `WRT` is `$ADV/tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts`, `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and `BG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`. `MARK` is the file name `skilled-behaviour-arena`.\n38: - WG3: `CAP` is `$RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `SLT` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`. `ENV9` is the nine names `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC`, `VITEST`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW` and `SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS`.\n39: - WG4: `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `CTS` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`.\n40: - WG5: `PB` is `$SKA/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `PBT` is `$ADV/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and `TR` is `$ADV/tests/README.md`.\n41: - WG6: `PJ` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `PJT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `ENV` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`.\n42: - WG7: `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`, `SUBT` is `$ADV/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and `ARM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`.\n43: - WG8: `DAE` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`, `RTS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`, `DAC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs` and `DSCT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs`.\n44: - WG9: `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `HWT` is `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`.\n45: - WG10: `PS` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`.\n46: - `SP` holds this phase's records and `PL` holds the 18 planning probes. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it, and each builds and removes its own temporary trees.\n47: \n48: Rules for every task:\n49: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs. A task that says its case passes today adds a guard and changes no code.\n50: - Re-read every file a task names before the first edit. Phase 016 edited some of them after this plan was written. When a line, string or name the task quotes is not in the file, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the line found in its place.\n51: - No test input or expected output names `/create:skill` or `/create:sk-skill`. Use `/create:agent` or `/create:readme`.\n52: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`, and no task opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n53: - No worker runs a build, the full suite, a daemon or a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under the system temp folder and removes them.\n54: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T040 checks it.\n55: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, `PS`, another phase folder, any `package.json`, any routing corpus, any committed baseline or a file another lane owns. Add no dependency.\n56: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. A doc sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\n57: - Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n58: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n59: \n60: Worker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. The lanes own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n61: - Setup, the coordinator: T001, T002.\n62: - Wave 1, nine worker lanes and the coordinator, all in parallel after T002. WG1: T003, T004, T005, T006, T007, T008, T009. WG2: T010, T011, T012, T013. WG3: T014, T015. WG4: T016, T017, T018, T019, T020, T021. WG5: T022, T023, T024. WG6: T025, T026, T027, T028. WG7: T029, T030. WG8: T031, T032, T033. WG9: T034, T035. Coordinator: T036.\n63: - Verification, one at a time after every wave 1 lane ends: T037, T038, T039, T040, T041, all `[C]`.\n64: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n69: ## Phase 1: Setup\n70: \n71: - [x] T001 [C] Confirm phase 016 is committed and record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `G log -1 --format=%h -- .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `test -e .skilled/commands/create/skill.md`, `G status --porcelain -- .skilled .opencode AGENTS.md` and `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, then `npm run build` in `ADV`, `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `A10Q`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its last output lines or its exit code into `before.txt`. When phase 016 is not committed or a gate is red, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. Verify: the `log` prints a hash, `test -e` exits 1, the `status` prints nothing, the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `FLOOR` prints typed recall `correct` at least 24 of 44, false offers `count` 0 of 35, typed `combined` 44 of 44 and plain tune `combined` at least 23 of 45, `EVAL` prints no value below `[160,50,21]` in its first three places and a fourth no higher than 5, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 17.\n72: - [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run each of the 18 probes in `PL` as its first comment line says, with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset, and append each command, its output and its exit code. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> \"/create:agent\"' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> true' -e 'fake CLI ran: true, fake hook ran: true' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md true, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm pre' -e 'run line records the fixture: false' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=1' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode NON_ZERO_EXIT, retriesAttempted 0' -e 'bash -lc: exit 1 hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 0' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: no' -e 'privacy case persists a record: false' -e 'LF: raw break in literal true, parses false' -e 'variables left changed: [\"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\"' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: false' -e 'note: the source category tree contains 41' -e 'handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563 =>' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 17 and every recorded exit code is 0.\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n78: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n79: \n80: ### Wave 1, lane WG1: the shared no-edit gate and bridge text\n81: - [x] T003 [P] Widen the shared no-edit pattern and add `isNoEditRequest` (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a no-edit prompt')`, add `it.each(NOEDIT4)('offers no hub command when the prompt ends %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-agent'), 'use sk-doc to create an agent called invoice-parser, ' + ending)` to be `undefined`, add `it('offers the agent command when the prompt asks for the change')` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-agent'), 'use sk-doc to create an agent called invoice-parser')` to be `'/create:agent'`, and add `it('reads a curly apostrophe as a straight one')` expecting `isNoEditRequest('Don\\u2019t touch any files')` to be `true` and `isNoEditRequest('touch the files')` to be `false`, importing `isNoEditRequest` beside `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four `it.each` cases return `'/create:agent'` and the helper case fail. Then in `CA` replace the `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` literal with `/\\b(no edits?|no changes|without making changes|(?:do not|don't) (change|edit|modify|touch)|read-only only|no edits yet|only; do not|just show|just list)\\b/`, add below it `export function isNoEditRequest(text: string): boolean` returning `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(text.toLowerCase().replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\"))` with a comment that many keyboards type the contraction with a curly apostrophe, and replace `if (NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())) return undefined;` in `attachCommand` with `if (isNoEditRequest(prompt)) return undefined;`. Verify: the first `VX` run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing.\n82: - [x] T004 [P] Route the explainer test through the shared helper (`TX`, `ROE`). Test first: in `ROE`, add `it.each([...])('treats a read-only request that rules out a change as read-only: %s', ...)` over `please show me the parser config, don't change anything yet`, `please show me the parser config so i can update it later, no changes yet`, `please show me what the fix would be, don\\u2019t touch any files` and `please show me the parser config and what to edit, make no changes`, each expecting `isReadOnlyExplainer(prompt.toLowerCase())` to be `true`. Run `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and see all four return `false`. Then in `TX` add `import { isNoEditRequest } from '../command-attach.js';` below the module header and replace the line that starts `const explicitNoWrite = /\\b(no edits?|without making changes|` with `const explicitNoWrite = isNoEditRequest(promptLower);`. Verify: the first run fails four cases, then `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"without making changes\" $TX` prints nothing.\n83: - [x] T005 [P] Route the scorer's two command gates through the shared helper (`FU`, `CMA`). Test first: in `CMA`, inside `describe('commandMeaningEligible')`, add `it('rules out every command when the prompt asks for no change with a curly apostrophe')` with the prompt `'walk me through the optional behaviour toggles, don\\u2019t touch anything'`, expecting `commandMeaningEligible(prompt, false, mutatingCommand)` and `commandMeaningEligible(prompt, false, readOnlyCommand)` to be `false`. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see the new case return `true`. Then in `FU` replace `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` with `isNoEditRequest` in the import from `'../command-attach.js'`, and replace both `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(promptLower)` calls, the one in `readOnlyRouteAllowed` and the one in `commandMeaningEligible`, with `isNoEditRequest(promptLower)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"isNoEditRequest\\(promptLower\\)\" $FU` prints 2, `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0.\n84: - [x] T006 [P] Make the status privacy case store what it guards (`AST`). Keep the case name `does not leak prompt content in status output`. After `writeGeneration(root, 'live', 5);`, save `process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, set it to `'1'`, await `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({ runtime: 'claude', status: 'ok', freshness: 'live', durationMs: 10, cacheHit: true, skillLabel: 'privacy-marker-skill', errorDetails: 'secret@example.com' }))` and restore the variable in a `finally`, as the case `reports hook health from durable diagnostic records` does. Then expect `readFileSync(advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root), 'utf8')` to contain `privacy-marker-skill` and `secret@example.com`, keep the two `not.toContain` lines on `raw`, add `expect(raw).not.toContain('privacy-marker-skill')` and expect `JSON.parse(raw).data.hookHealth.invocations` to be 1. This case passes today, because status carries aggregates only, and it guards that. Verify: `VX tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node TSX $PL/probe-status-privacy.mts` prints `privacy case persists a record: true`.\n85: - [x] T007 [P] Drop the attach assertion that never reaches a gate (`CAT`). In the case `offers a deep-loop command only when the prompt asks for that effort`, delete the line `expect(attachCommand('sk-doc', singleRoute('sk-create-benchmark'), PLAIN_PROMPT, INJECTED)).toBeUndefined();` and keep the next line, which proves the gate belongs to the deep-loop hub alone. Verify: `rg -c \"singleRoute\\('sk-create-benchmark'\\), PLAIN_PROMPT\" $CAT` prints nothing and `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n86: - [x] T008 [P] Name every command row field in the command-bridges README (`CBR`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('generated command table')`, add `it('the command-bridges README names every command row field')`, which reads `join(import.meta.dirname, '../lib/command-attach.ts')` and `join(import.meta.dirname, '../scripts/command-bridges/README.md')` with `readFileSync` (import it from `node:fs` and `join` from `node:path` when absent), takes the field names from the `export interface CommandRow {` block with `/readonly (\\w+)\\??:/g`, expects them to equal `['command', 'policy', 'mutating', 'ownerSkillId']` and expects the README sentence that starts `Each row carries` to contain each name wrapped in backticks. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the first name. Then in `CBR` replace the sentence `Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill.` with ``Each row carries `command`, the runnable slash command, `policy`, its derived policy, `mutating`, the class that says what a run writes (`read-only`, `add-only` or `mutates`) when the record names one, and `ownerSkillId`, the owning skill.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c \"its derived policy and the owning skill\" $CBR` prints nothing.\n87: - [x] T009 [P] Escape line breaks in generated string literals (`DER`, `DCS`). Test first: create `DCS` with the module banner the other test files use and a comment saying a generated literal holding a raw line break no longer parses, so the generated source would stop compiling. Load `DER` with `createRequire(import.meta.url)` as `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` does, and add `it.each([['LF', 'a\\nb'], ['CR', 'a\\rb'], ['U+2028', 'a\\u2028b'], ['U+2029', 'a\\u2029b'], ['a quote and a backslash', \"it's a \\\\ path\"]])('round-trips a value holding %s', (_label, value) => ...)`, expecting `tsString(value)` to match `/^'[^\\n\\r\\u2028\\u2029]*'$/` and `new Function('return ' + tsString(value) + ';')()` to equal `value`. Run `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` and see it fail because `tsString` is not exported. Then in `DER` add `tsString` to `module.exports`, and in `tsString` chain `.replaceAll('\\n', '\\\\n').replaceAll('\\r', '\\\\r').replaceAll('\\u2028', '\\\\u2028').replaceAll('\\u2029', '\\\\u2029')` after the two existing `replaceAll` calls. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `node $PL/probe-tsstring.cjs` prints `exported: true` and `parses true` on its four break lines.\n88: \n89: ### Wave 1, lane WG2: behaviour runner replay and restore\n90: - [x] T010 [P] Run no code from an untrusted backfill checkout (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('runs nothing from a checkout that is neither the project root nor a marked arena')`: make a temporary folder holding a fake `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` and a fake `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, each writing its own marker file into that folder when run, write a one-line log whose `locator.projectDir` names the folder, call `backfillRunLog` with `promptFor: () => 'prompt'`, `brief: async () => 'unknown'` and the default warm and replay, and expect `ok` true, `lines` 1, `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` on the written line and neither marker file. Add `it('replays a checkout that holds the arena marker')`, where the folder also holds `.git/skilled-behaviour-arena` and stub `warm` and `replay` record their `checkoutDir`, expecting both to record that folder. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the first case fail because both fakes ran. Then in `CO` add `realpathSync` to the `node:fs` import and `export function trustedCheckout(checkoutDir)`, which returns `true` when `realpathSync(checkoutDir)` equals `realpathSync(REPO_ROOT)` or `existsSync(join(checkoutDir, '.git', 'skilled-behaviour-arena'))` holds, and `false` when either call throws, with a comment that a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Give `backfillRunLog` a `trusted = trustedCheckout` option, named in its jsdoc, and before the warm-up, when `checkoutDir !== null && !trusted(checkoutDir)`, set the offer to `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'untrusted_checkout' }` and skip the warm-up and the replay. In the existing case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once`, pass `trusted: () => true`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-backfill-tru... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n91: - [x] T011 [P] Read NUL-separated status in the restore (`WR`, `WRT`). Test first: in `WRT`, add `it('removes a created file whose name holds a space')`, which takes a `statusSnapshot` of `makeRepository()`, writes `notes draft.md` and `plain.md`, and expects `restoreTurn` to return `restored: true` with `leftoverPaths` empty and both files gone, and add `it('keys both sides of a rename whose new name holds a space')`, which runs `git mv kept.txt 'renamed file.txt'` after the snapshot and expects the next snapshot's keys to include `renamed file.txt` and `kept.txt` and `restoreTurn` to return `restored: true`. Run `VX tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and see both fail on the quoted name. Then in `WR` make `statusSnapshot` run `status --porcelain -z`, split stdout on `'\\0'`, take each entry's code from its first two characters and its path from the fourth character on, and when the code holds `R` or `C` take the next field as the source path under the same code, with the jsdoc saying the NUL form never quotes a path. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-restore-quoted.mjs` prints `left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false`.\n92: - [x] T012 [P] Run a started-command row picked by id under arm g2 (`R`, `BG`). Test first: in `BG`, import `armFor` from the runner and add `describe('armFor')` expecting `armFor({ arm: null, set: null }, ['g2-deep-review-ask'])` to be `'g2'`, `armFor({ arm: null, set: 'g2' }, G2_ROWS.map((row) => row.id))` to be `'g2'`, `armFor({ arm: 'post', set: null }, ['g2-deep-review-ask'])` to be `'post'`, `armFor({ arm: null, set: null }, ['cmd-x'])` and `armFor({ arm: null, set: null }, [])` to be `'pre'`, and `armFor({ arm: null, set: null }, ['g2-deep-review-ask', 'cmd-x'])` to throw an error whose `code` is `mixed_row_arms`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail because `armFor` is not exported. Then in `R` make it `export function armFor(options, rowIds)`: an explicit `options.arm` wins, ids that are all `G2_ROWS` ids give `G2_SET`, ids that hold none give `DEFAULT_ARM` and a mix throws `new Refusal('mixed_row_arms', ...)` naming the started-command ids, with the comment saying a started-command row joins its own comparison whichever flag picked it. In `main`, change `options.arm = armFor(options);` to `options.arm = armFor(options, rowIds);`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2` and `--row-id g2-deep-review-ask --row-id cmd-x -> arm refused mixed_row_arms`.\n93: - [x] T013 [P] Record the fixture on a g2 run line and replay it (`R`, `CO`, `BG`, `COT`). Test first: in `BG`, import `lineFixture` and expect `lineFixture({ fixture: '/custom/fixture' }, '/runs/arm/g2-fixture')` to be `'/custom/fixture'` and `lineFixture({}, '/runs/arm/g2-fixture')` and `lineFixture({ fixture: '' }, '/runs/arm/g2-fixture')` to be `'/runs/arm/g2-fixture'`. In `COT`, add `it('hands each line to the prompt lookup')`, whose `promptFor` records its second argument for a line carrying `fixture: '/custom/fixture'`, with `trusted: () => true` and stub warm, replay and brief, expecting the recorded line's `fixture` to be `'/custom/fixture'`. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see both fail. Then in `CO` call `promptFor(row.rowId, row)` and say in its jsdoc that the lookup also receives the line. In `R` add `export function lineFixture(line, fallback)`, which returns `line.fixture` when it is a non-empty string and `fallback` otherwise, and in `backfillLog` pass `promptFor: (rowId, line) => promptFor(rowId, lineFixture(line, fixture))`. In `runArm`, add `fixture` to the job when `G2_ROWS` holds the row id, and in `runTurn` add `...(job.fixture === undefined ? {} : { fixture: job.fixture }),` inside the `const line = {` object. Verify: both first runs fail as described, then both files report 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs` prints `run line records the fixture: true` and `its backfill replays: review the parser under /custom/fixture for correctness gaps and write up what you find, one iteration is enough`.\n94: \n95: ### Wave 1, lane WG3: measurement environment hygiene\n96: - [x] T014 [P] Restore every variable the capture sets or deletes (`CAP`, `SLT`). Test first: in `SLT`, inside `beforeAll`, copy the `ENV9` values from `process.env` into `envBefore` before `scoreCommandCorpus()` and into `envAfter` after it, and add `it('leaves the caller environment as it found it')` expecting `envAfter` to equal `envBefore`. Run `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` and see the new case fail on `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`. Then in `CAP`, at the start of `scoreCommandCorpus` and before its `try`, save each `ENV9` value or its absence, and in the `finally`, after `globalThis.Date = RealDate;`, set each saved value back and delete each name that was absent, with a comment saying a harness imports this module and scores in process, so the projection must not outlive the call. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node $PL/probe-capture-env.mjs` prints `variables left changed: []`.\n97: - [x] T015 [P] Measure the parent brief from a dispatched worker (`MBC`, `MBCT`). Test first: in `MBCT`, let `HOOK_STUB` write `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD ?? '<unset>'` to the file that `CHILD_PROBE_FILE` names, only when that variable is set, so the existing cases are unchanged. When `runScript` takes no environment argument, add `env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env` as its second parameter and pass it to `spawnSync`. Add `it('runs each hook child without the dispatched-child flag')`, which runs the script with `--root <root> --rows cost-live` and an environment holding `AI_SESSION_CHILD: '1'` and `CHILD_PROBE_FILE` inside the test root, and expects that file to read `<unset>`. Run `VX tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` and see it read `1`. Then in `MBC`'s `measureRow`, build the object it passes as `env` into `const env`, `delete env.AI_SESSION_CHILD` and pass `env`, with a comment saying the script measures what the operator's own session receives. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-cost-child.mjs` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>`.\n98: \n99: ### Wave 1, lane WG4: transcript scorer and routing-accuracy README\n100: - [x] T016 [P] Refuse `--row-id` in the scorer's session form (`S`, `CTS`). Test first: in `CTS`, inside `describe('reader failure')`, add `it('refuses a row id in the session form')`, which runs `runScorer(['--runtime', 'claude', '--locator', '{\"sessionId\":\"session-1\"}', '--row-id', 'no-such-row'])` and expects status 2, an empty stdout and a stderr containing `--row-id narrows --summary only`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see stdout read `{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"locator_unavailable\"}`. Then in `S`'s `selectMode`, after the `--runtime` and `--locator` checks, throw `new UsageError('--row-id narrows --summary only')` when `options.rowId !== null`, and remove ` [--row-id <id>]` from the `--runtime` usage line in the header comment and in `USAGE`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c -e '--locator .*\\[--row-id' $S` prints nothing.\n101: - [x] T017 [P] Describe what the scorer prints (`S`). Replace the three header comment lines `// Reads a captured session through the shared session readers and reports what a`, ``// model did with the commands a turn offered it: the `COMMAND:` lines it printed,`` and `// the reads and writes in order, and whether a started loop ran its init first.` with `// Reads captured sessions through the shared session readers and prints counts`, `// and verdicts per runtime and arm: how often an offered command was started,` and `// seen or declined, which runs were unsafe and which started loops skipped their init.` Verify: `rg -c \"the reads and writes in order\" $S` prints nothing, `rg -c \"and verdicts per runtime and arm\" $S` prints 1 and `node --check $S` exits 0.\n102: - [x] T018 [P] Say where `--row-id` applies (`RA`). In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, replace `` `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row `` with `` `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime` ``. Verify: `rg -c \"narrows either mode\" $RA` prints nothing and `rg -c \"is a usage error with\" $RA` prints 1.\n103: - [x] T019 [P] Document the untrusted backfill checkout (`RA`). After the sentence that starts `A line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields`, add ``A line whose checkout is neither this project root nor an arena holding the `skilled-behaviour-arena` marker also keeps null offer fields, with `offerError` `untrusted_checkout`, because a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Nothing from that folder runs, and the rest of the log is still written.`` In the `command-offer.mjs` row, replace `with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input.` with ``with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena.`` Verify: `rg -c \"untrusted_checkout\" $RA` prints 1 and `rg -c \"trustedCheckout\" $RA` prints 1.\n104: - [x] T020 [P] Document the g2 arm rule and the recorded fixture (`RA`). In the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row, after ``optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`.`` add ``Without `--arm`, a selection whose ids are all started-command rows runs under arm `g2`, one that holds none runs under `pre` and a mix is refused with `mixed_row_arms`. Each `g2` run line records the `fixture` folder its prompt named, and `--backfill` replays that folder, or `g2-fixture` beside the log for a line that holds none.`` In the same row's exit-2 list, after `` a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), `` add `` a selection that mixes started-command rows with others (`mixed_row_arms`), ``. Verify: `rg -o \"mixed_row_arms\" $RA | wc -l` prints 2 and `rg -c \"folder its prompt named\" $RA` prints 1.\n105: - [x] T021 [P] Document the cost script's child flag (`RA`). In the `Sandbox:` bullet under `measure-brief-cost.mjs`, add after its first sentence ``Each hook process also runs without `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so a run from a dispatched worker measures the brief an operator's own session receives rather than the child form.`` Verify: `rg -c \"rather than the child form\" $RA` prints 1.\n106: \n107: ### Wave 1, lane WG5: playbook and tests README\n108: - [x] T022 [P] State the playbook inventory from the tree (`PB`, `PBT`). Test first: in `PBT`, inside the case `keeps the root playbook aligned with the live 50-scenario corpus`, expect `files.filter((file) => /\\/\\d{3}-[^/]*\\.md$/.test(file))` to have length 0, expect `markdown` to contain `The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them` and expect it not to contain `scenario files plus no`. Run `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the new sentence. Then in `PB` replace ``The source root index describes 42 scenarios, but the source category tree contains 41 `NNN-*.md` scenario files plus no `CL-002`.`` with ``The source root index describes 42 scenarios. The category tree holds 50 scenario files named by feature, none of them `NNN-*.md`, and still no `CL-002`.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n109: - [x] T023 [P] Name the folder scenario results are written to by hand (`PB`, `PBT`). Test first: in `PBT`, add `it('names the folder scenario results are recorded in by hand')`, expecting `markdown` to contain `<!-- MANUAL_PLAYBOOK_RESULT_PERSISTENCE_CONTRACT -->`, `recorded by hand in` and `system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`, and not to contain `renderer-owned`. Run `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and see it fail on `recorded by hand in`. Then in `PB`, keep the marker line and replace the paragraph below it with ``A scenario run is complete only after its `PASS`, `FAIL` or `SKIP` outcome, its reason and its evidence paths are recorded by hand in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/benchmark/reports/<dated-run-label>/`. The first recorded run creates that folder, because the wrapper that once wrote these records was retired and no renderer writes them now.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n110: - [x] T024 [P] Describe the playbook test as the inventory test it is (`TR`). Replace the row ``| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures. |`` with ``| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Checks the playbook inventory: the root playbook lists every scenario file in the category tree once, and its persistence note names the folder results are recorded in. |`` Verify: `rg -c \"Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures\" $TR` prints nothing and `rg -c \"Checks the playbook inventory\" $TR` prints 1.\n111: \n112: ### Wave 1, lane WG6: OpenCode plugin residue and field tests\n113: - [x] T025 [P] Correct the bounding option's jsdoc (`PJ`). Replace ` * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Bound long compiled-route target lists` with ` * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Reported as the bounded_compiled_route_summary status field. The brief carries no compiled-route line, so it bounds nothing`. Verify: `rg -c \"Bound long compiled-route target lists\" $PJ` prints nothing, `node --check $PJ` exits 0 and `VP` reports `fail 0`.\n114: - [x] T026 [P] Remove the route summary nothing reads (`PJ`). Delete the function `compiledRouteSummary(data)` with the comment block above it, the line `const routeSummary = compiledRouteSummary(data);` and the line `...(routeSummary ? { compiledRouteSummary: routeSummary } : {}),` in the returned metadata. Verify: `rg -c \"compiledRouteSummary\" $PJ` prints nothing, `node --check $PJ` exits 0 and `VP` reports `fail 0`.\n115: - [x] T027 [P] Test the command fields on the plugin path (`PJT`). Add `test('renders the command, its policy and its owner from the advisor row')`, which saves and deletes `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD`, builds the plugin with `makePlugin({ spawnOverride: spawnSequence([fakeChild({ stdout: cliEnvelope({ recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', score: 0.9, confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }) })]) })`, awaits `runPrompt(hooks)`, restores the variable in a `finally` and asserts that `output.system[0]` contains `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when the plugin drops a field. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0` and `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node TSX $PL/probe-plugin-fields.mts` prints `plugin test asserts a command label: true`.\n116: - [x] T028 [P] Test the command fields on the fallback path (`ENV`). Add `it('keeps the command, its policy and its owner from a CLI row')`, which calls `resultFromCliData` with `data: { freshness: 'live', recommendations: [{ skillId: 'sk-doc', confidence: 0.95, uncertainty: 0.12, command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }] }` and the `options`, `startedAt` and `now` the existing cases pass, expects `result.recommendations[0]` to match `{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc' }` and expects the first line of `renderAdvisorBrief(result)` to contain `sk-doc → /create:agent (start)`. This case passes today and fails when a field is dropped. Verify: `VX tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n117: \n118: ### Wave 1, lane WG7: subprocess busy scan and catalog anchors\n119: - [x] T029 [P] See a busy marker past the stderr cap (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: in `SUBT`, rename the case `stops reading stderr at the cap, so a busy marker past it is not seen` to `retries once on a busy marker written after the cap`, expect `errorCode` `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` and `retriesAttempted` 1, and replace the comment above it with one saying the cap bounds what is kept, not what is scanned. Add `it('retries once on a busy marker split across two writes after the cap')`, whose child writes `'e'.repeat(1024 * 1024)`, then `'\\ndatabase is '`, waits 20 ms, writes `'locked\\n'` and exits 1, expecting the same two values, so neither write alone holds the marker. Run `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and see both report `NON_ZERO_EXIT`. Then in `SUB` add `readonly sawBusy: boolean;` to `SpawnAttemptResult`, keep a `busyCarry` string and a `sawBusy` flag in `runSpawnAttempt`, and in the stderr `data` handler, before `capOutput`, test `SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN` against `busyCarry + chunk` until it matches, keeping the last 64 characters as the next `busyCarry`. Report `sawBusy` in every `resolve` call and read the retry decision as `attemptResult.sawBusy || SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/legacy/advisor-subprocess.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `node TSX $PL/probe-busy-cap.mts` prints `marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1`.\n120: - [x] T030 [P] Cite the catalog's schema and handler anchors by name (`ARM`). Replace `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:308` `` with ``the `compiledRoute` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` `` with ``the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634` `` with ``the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` ``, and each of `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` `` and `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290` `` with ``the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``. Leave the citations of `lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, `tools/advisor-recommend.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts`. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendationSchema\" $ARM` prints 3, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\" $ARM` prints 2 and `bash $PL/probe-catalog-lines.sh` prints no `advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and no `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` line.\n121: \n122: ### Wave 1, lane WG8: doctor embed and setup contracts\n123: - [x] T031 [P] Give a failed restore its own exit-3 outcome (`DAE`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')`, which takes the one line of `EMBED_YAML` that contains `Exit 3 means` and asserts it matches `/ERROR: the restore failed/`, `/quote both ERROR lines/` and `/takes precedence over the restored: outcome/`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on the first pattern. Then in `DAE`, inside the same quoted string that starts `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup.`, append `When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0 and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `workflow names the restore failure: 1`.\n124: - [x] T032 [P] Name the backup folder by the plan digest (`DAE`, `RTS`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow and route name the backup folder the engine makes')`, asserting that `EMBED_YAML` and `routeFor('embed').gate3_location` each contain `doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/` and not `<timestamp>`, and that the route text contains `temporary directory`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on `<timestamp>`. Then in `DAE` replace `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/` with `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/`, and in `RTS`, inside the embed route's `gate3_location`, replace `taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte` with `taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes`.\n125: - [x] T033 [P] Give the setup router the workflow's reason for absent hook health (`DSM`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, inside `test('the setup workflow and router both name the unrecorded hook health state'`, add `assert.match(SETUP_ROUTER, /because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet/)` and `assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/)`. Run `NT $DSCT` and see it fail on the first assertion. Then in `DSM` replace ``When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.`` with `When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `RV` and `SRM` exit 0.\n126: \n127: ### Wave 1, lane WG9: doctor check scripts\n128: - [x] T034 [P] Read a hook command the way a shell runs it (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: in `HWT`, add one `test` per launch that writes `writeClaudeSettings(f.root, { UserPromptSubmit: [{ hooks: [{ type: 'command', command }] }] })` and expects exit 0 and `ok claude`, for the commands `` `env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `/usr/bin/env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `bash -lc \"node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``, `` `zsh -c 'node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}'` ``, `` `node --no-warnings ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `cd \"$PWD\"&& node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` `` and `` `cd /tmp; node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, and one more that expects exit 1 and `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` for `` `echo \"x && node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``. Run `NT $HWT` and see the seven launches print `hook-missing` and the `echo` case print `ok`. Then in `HW` replace `stripQuotes`, `startsCommand` and the body of `runsMarker(command, marker)` with a reader that splits the command into words outside quotes, honouring single quotes, double quotes and a backslash escape, and ends a simple command at `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|` or a newline outside quotes, even one stuck to a word. A simple command is wired when, after any leading `NAME=value` words, its first word is `node` or a path ending `/node` and its first word after any words starting `-` ends with the marker. A first word of `env` or a path ending `/env` is dropped with the `NAME=value` and `-` words after it before that test. A first word of `bash`, `sh` or `zsh`, or a path ending in one, followed by a word that starts with a single `-` and holds `c`, makes the word after it a script that is read again as commands, at most two levels deep. A quoted word is otherwise only an argument, so an `echo` of a quoted script stays unwired. Keep the comment saying a mention is not a wired hook. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with every existing case unchanged, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin`, and `n... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n129: - [x] T035 [P] Count only verified copies as expected in A10 (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, in the case `A10 leaves a missing pointer out of the count and names it after the copies`, replace the assertion that the detail matches `/^5\\/6 copies as expected/u` with `assert.equal(copies.detail, '3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing', ...)`. Run `NT $CHKT` and see it print `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing`. Then in `CHK`'s `rowRuntimeCopies`, count as expected only the entries whose `state` is `PASS`, count as reported only the `INFO` entries whose `kind` is not `pointer missing`, and build the detail as `<expected>/<total> copies as expected` followed by `, <n> unmeasured`, `, <n> reported only` and `, <n> pointer missing`, each only when its count is above 0. Leave the row's state rule as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `A10Q` prints a detail whose first number equals its `pass` count and whose `reported only` number equals its `reported` count, which reads `3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` while the manifest holds the six entries it held at planning.\n130: \n131: ### Wave 1, coordinator: the parent phase map\n132: - [x] T036 [C] Correct three rows of the parent phase map (`PS`). Re-read `PS` and the status rows of the 007, 014 and 015 child specs first. In row 7, after `(R8 transcripts, G2, G5)` add `. It stays open until the final behaviour arm, run on fresh arenas after the merge to main by operator instruction of 2026-11-13, settles T020, T046 and the acceptance rows AC-004, AC-005 and AC-007`. Set the Status cell of rows 14 and 15 to `Complete`. Change no other row. Verify: `bash $PL/probe-phase-map.sh | rg -e '^row (7|14|15) ' | rg -c differs` prints nothing and `rg -c \"until the final behaviour arm\" $PS` prints 1.\n133: \n134: ### Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\n135: Two independent verifiers read the wave 1 diff (`$SP/verify-wg1-4.md`, `$SP/verify-wg5-9.md`): 33 of 33 tasks do what their line says, no P0 or P1 and nine P2. The four below were built by the coordinator. Four were left: the g2 run-line write in `R` has no suite test and stays covered by `$PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs`, which T039 reruns. The literal marker path in `trustedCheckout` agrees with the arena builder and fails toward untrusted. A busy code split across two writes now counts as busy, which is a busy variant. The catalog pages of four other skills that name `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` belong to other skills and the advisor's hook path still carries that field, so they are outside this phase.\n136: - [x] T042 [C] Narrow the no-edit pattern so a change request that limits its scope keeps its command (`CA`, `CAG`). The bare `no changes` alternative read `refactor the parser so there are no changes to its public api` as a no-edit request. Replace it with `make no changes|no changes yet` and add an `it.each` of three scope-limiting change requests expecting `isNoEditRequest` to be `false`. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `rg -c \"make no changes\\|no changes yet\" $CA` prints 1.\n137: - [x] T043 [C] End the `--row-id` sentence before `--json` (`RA`). Verify: ``rg -c 'usage error with `--runtime`\\. `--json` prints' $RA`` prints 1.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 138]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 1-137\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 17: review-pass-two-remediation\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that fix the 27 P2 findings of review pass two in nine parallel worker lanes and one coordinator edit: the shared no-edit gate, the behaviour runner's backfill and restore, measurement hygiene, the scorer, playbook and plugin text, the subprocess busy scan, the doctor contracts and the doctor checks, each with a failing-then-passing test where one can exist.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review pass two remediation tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 17: review-pass-two-remediation\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a rebuild, a full-suite run, a parent spec edit or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says `in ADV`. A short name stands for the path or command below. Set the path names once with `export ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime RAD=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy SKA=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor DS=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts DA=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets SP=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch PL=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning`.\n30: - `G` is `git -c core.fsmonitor=false`. `BASE` is the commit T001 records with `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, so a diff against it covers committed and uncommitted lane work. `TSX` is `--import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs`, so `node TSX <file>` runs a TypeScript probe.\n31: - `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`, with `<file>` relative to `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n32: - `NT <file>` is `node --test <file>`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, `VSR` is `node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/*.test.mjs` and `VP` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, and each must report `fail 0`.\n33: - `DERIVE` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -c '{status, changed}'`, which must print `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`. `RV` is `bash $DS/route-validate.sh` and `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0. `PBV` is `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/scripts/validate-playbook-package.cjs --package $SKA/manual-testing-playbook`, which must print a line starting `PASS package=system-skill-advisor`.\n34: - `FLOOR` is `node $RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune'`, which printed `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` and `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` at planning. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which printed `[160,50,21,5]`. Phase 016 may change either, so T001 records the real before lines.\n35: - `A10Q` is `node $DS/agents-md-check.cjs --root . --json | jq -r '.rows[] | select(.id==\"A10\") | \"\\(.detail) | pass \\([.entries[] | select(.state==\"PASS\")] | length) | reported \\([.entries[] | select(.state==\"INFO\" and .kind!=\"pointer missing\")] | length)\"'`, which printed `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` at planning.\n36: - WG1: `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `TX` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/text.ts` and `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `CAG` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `ROE` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts`, `CMA` is `$ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `AST` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`. `DER` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` and `DCS` is `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` (new). `SINGLE(m)` is the helper `CAG` already defines, `{ action: 'route', selectionKind: 'single', targets: [{ workflowMode: m }] }`. `NOEDIT4` is the four endings `don't change anything yet`, `no changes yet`, `don\\u2019t touch any files` and `make no changes`, where `\\u2019` is written as that escape inside a test string, so the test holds a curly apostrophe and the source stays ASCII.\n37: - WG2: `CO` is `$RAD/command-offer.mjs`, `COT` is `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`, `WR` is `$RAD/worktree-restore.mjs`, `WRT` is `$ADV/tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts`, `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and `BG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`. `MARK` is the file name `skilled-behaviour-arena`.\n38: - WG3: `CAP` is `$RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `SLT` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`. `ENV9` is the nine names `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC`, `VITEST`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW` and `SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS`.\n39: - WG4: `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `CTS` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`.\n40: - WG5: `PB` is `$SKA/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `PBT` is `$ADV/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and `TR` is `$ADV/tests/README.md`.\n41: - WG6: `PJ` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `PJT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `ENV` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`.\n42: - WG7: `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`, `SUBT` is `$ADV/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and `ARM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`.\n43: - WG8: `DAE` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`, `RTS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`, `DAC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs` and `DSCT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs`.\n44: - WG9: `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `HWT` is `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`.\n45: - WG10: `PS` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`.\n46: - `SP` holds this phase's records and `PL` holds the 18 planning probes. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it, and each builds and removes its own temporary trees.\n47: \n48: Rules for every task:\n49: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs. A task that says its case passes today adds a guard and changes no code.\n50: - Re-read every file a task names before the first edit. Phase 016 edited some of them after this plan was written. When a line, string or name the task quotes is not in the file, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the line found in its place.\n51: - No test input or expected output names `/create:skill` or `/create:sk-skill`. Use `/create:agent` or `/create:readme`.\n52: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`, and no task opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n53: - No worker runs a build, the full suite, a daemon or a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under the system temp folder and removes them.\n54: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T040 checks it.\n55: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, `PS`, another phase folder, any `package.json`, any routing corpus, any committed baseline or a file another lane owns. Add no dependency.\n56: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. A doc sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\n57: - Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n58: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n59: \n60: Worker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. The lanes own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n61: - Setup, the coordinator: T001, T002.\n62: - Wave 1, nine worker lanes and the coordinator, all in parallel after T002. WG1: T003, T004, T005, T006, T007, T008, T009. WG2: T010, T011, T012, T013. WG3: T014, T015. WG4: T016, T017, T018, T019, T020, T021. WG5: T022, T023, T024. WG6: T025, T026, T027, T028. WG7: T029, T030. WG8: T031, T032, T033. WG9: T034, T035. Coordinator: T036.\n63: - Verification, one at a time after every wave 1 lane ends: T037, T038, T039, T040, T041, all `[C]`.\n64: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n69: ## Phase 1: Setup\n70: \n71: - [x] T001 [C] Confirm phase 016 is committed and record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `G log -1 --format=%h -- .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `test -e .skilled/commands/create/skill.md`, `G status --porcelain -- .skilled .opencode AGENTS.md` and `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, then `npm run build` in `ADV`, `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `A10Q`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its last output lines or its exit code into `before.txt`. When phase 016 is not committed or a gate is red, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. Verify: the `log` prints a hash, `test -e` exits 1, the `status` prints nothing, the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `FLOOR` prints typed recall `correct` at least 24 of 44, false offers `count` 0 of 35, typed `combined` 44 of 44 and plain tune `combined` at least 23 of 45, `EVAL` prints no value below `[160,50,21]` in its first three places and a fourth no higher than 5, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 17.\n72: - [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run each of the 18 probes in `PL` as its first comment line says, with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset, and append each command, its output and its exit code. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> \"/create:agent\"' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> true' -e 'fake CLI ran: true, fake hook ran: true' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md true, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm pre' -e 'run line records the fixture: false' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=1' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode NON_ZERO_EXIT, retriesAttempted 0' -e 'bash -lc: exit 1 hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 0' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: no' -e 'privacy case persists a record: false' -e 'LF: raw break in literal true, parses false' -e 'variables left changed: [\"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\"' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: false' -e 'note: the source category tree contains 41' -e 'handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563 =>' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 17 and every recorded exit code is 0.\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n78: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n79: \n80: ### Wave 1, lane WG1: the shared no-edit gate and bridge text\n81: - [x] T003 [P] Widen the shared no-edit pattern and add `isNoEditRequest` (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a no-edit prompt')`, add `it.each(NOEDIT4)('offers no hub command when the prompt ends %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-agent'), 'use sk-doc to create an agent called invoice-parser, ' + ending)` to be `undefined`, add `it('offers the agent command when the prompt asks for the change')` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-agent'), 'use sk-doc to create an agent called invoice-parser')` to be `'/create:agent'`, and add `it('reads a curly apostrophe as a straight one')` expecting `isNoEditRequest('Don\\u2019t touch any files')` to be `true` and `isNoEditRequest('touch the files')` to be `false`, importing `isNoEditRequest` beside `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four `it.each` cases return `'/create:agent'` and the helper case fail. Then in `CA` replace the `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` literal with `/\\b(no edits?|no changes|without making changes|(?:do not|don't) (change|edit|modify|touch)|read-only only|no edits yet|only; do not|just show|just list)\\b/`, add below it `export function isNoEditRequest(text: string): boolean` returning `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(text.toLowerCase().replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\"))` with a comment that many keyboards type the contraction with a curly apostrophe, and replace `if (NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())) return undefined;` in `attachCommand` with `if (isNoEditRequest(prompt)) return undefined;`. Verify: the first `VX` run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing.\n82: - [x] T004 [P] Route the explainer test through the shared helper (`TX`, `ROE`). Test first: in `ROE`, add `it.each([...])('treats a read-only request that rules out a change as read-only: %s', ...)` over `please show me the parser config, don't change anything yet`, `please show me the parser config so i can update it later, no changes yet`, `please show me what the fix would be, don\\u2019t touch any files` and `please show me the parser config and what to edit, make no changes`, each expecting `isReadOnlyExplainer(prompt.toLowerCase())` to be `true`. Run `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and see all four return `false`. Then in `TX` add `import { isNoEditRequest } from '../command-attach.js';` below the module header and replace the line that starts `const explicitNoWrite = /\\b(no edits?|without making changes|` with `const explicitNoWrite = isNoEditRequest(promptLower);`. Verify: the first run fails four cases, then `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"without making changes\" $TX` prints nothing.\n83: - [x] T005 [P] Route the scorer's two command gates through the shared helper (`FU`, `CMA`). Test first: in `CMA`, inside `describe('commandMeaningEligible')`, add `it('rules out every command when the prompt asks for no change with a curly apostrophe')` with the prompt `'walk me through the optional behaviour toggles, don\\u2019t touch anything'`, expecting `commandMeaningEligible(prompt, false, mutatingCommand)` and `commandMeaningEligible(prompt, false, readOnlyCommand)` to be `false`. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see the new case return `true`. Then in `FU` replace `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` with `isNoEditRequest` in the import from `'../command-attach.js'`, and replace both `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(promptLower)` calls, the one in `readOnlyRouteAllowed` and the one in `commandMeaningEligible`, with `isNoEditRequest(promptLower)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"isNoEditRequest\\(promptLower\\)\" $FU` prints 2, `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0.\n84: - [x] T006 [P] Make the status privacy case store what it guards (`AST`). Keep the case name `does not leak prompt content in status output`. After `writeGeneration(root, 'live', 5);`, save `process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, set it to `'1'`, await `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({ runtime: 'claude', status: 'ok', freshness: 'live', durationMs: 10, cacheHit: true, skillLabel: 'privacy-marker-skill', errorDetails: 'secret@example.com' }))` and restore the variable in a `finally`, as the case `reports hook health from durable diagnostic records` does. Then expect `readFileSync(advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root), 'utf8')` to contain `privacy-marker-skill` and `secret@example.com`, keep the two `not.toContain` lines on `raw`, add `expect(raw).not.toContain('privacy-marker-skill')` and expect `JSON.parse(raw).data.hookHealth.invocations` to be 1. This case passes today, because status carries aggregates only, and it guards that. Verify: `VX tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node TSX $PL/probe-status-privacy.mts` prints `privacy case persists a record: true`.\n85: - [x] T007 [P] Drop the attach assertion that never reaches a gate (`CAT`). In the case `offers a deep-loop command only when the prompt asks for that effort`, delete the line `expect(attachCommand('sk-doc', singleRoute('sk-create-benchmark'), PLAIN_PROMPT, INJECTED)).toBeUndefined();` and keep the next line, which proves the gate belongs to the deep-loop hub alone. Verify: `rg -c \"singleRoute\\('sk-create-benchmark'\\), PLAIN_PROMPT\" $CAT` prints nothing and `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n86: - [x] T008 [P] Name every command row field in the command-bridges README (`CBR`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('generated command table')`, add `it('the command-bridges README names every command row field')`, which reads `join(import.meta.dirname, '../lib/command-attach.ts')` and `join(import.meta.dirname, '../scripts/command-bridges/README.md')` with `readFileSync` (import it from `node:fs` and `join` from `node:path` when absent), takes the field names from the `export interface CommandRow {` block with `/readonly (\\w+)\\??:/g`, expects them to equal `['command', 'policy', 'mutating', 'ownerSkillId']` and expects the README sentence that starts `Each row carries` to contain each name wrapped in backticks. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the first name. Then in `CBR` replace the sentence `Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill.` with ``Each row carries `command`, the runnable slash command, `policy`, its derived policy, `mutating`, the class that says what a run writes (`read-only`, `add-only` or `mutates`) when the record names one, and `ownerSkillId`, the owning skill.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c \"its derived policy and the owning skill\" $CBR` prints nothing.\n87: - [x] T009 [P] Escape line breaks in generated string literals (`DER`, `DCS`). Test first: create `DCS` with the module banner the other test files use and a comment saying a generated literal holding a raw line break no longer parses, so the generated source would stop compiling. Load `DER` with `createRequire(import.meta.url)` as `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` does, and add `it.each([['LF', 'a\\nb'], ['CR', 'a\\rb'], ['U+2028', 'a\\u2028b'], ['U+2029', 'a\\u2029b'], ['a quote and a backslash', \"it's a \\\\ path\"]])('round-trips a value holding %s', (_label, value) => ...)`, expecting `tsString(value)` to match `/^'[^\\n\\r\\u2028\\u2029]*'$/` and `new Function('return ' + tsString(value) + ';')()` to equal `value`. Run `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` and see it fail because `tsString` is not exported. Then in `DER` add `tsString` to `module.exports`, and in `tsString` chain `.replaceAll('\\n', '\\\\n').replaceAll('\\r', '\\\\r').replaceAll('\\u2028', '\\\\u2028').replaceAll('\\u2029', '\\\\u2029')` after the two existing `replaceAll` calls. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `node $PL/probe-tsstring.cjs` prints `exported: true` and `parses true` on its four break lines.\n88: \n89: ### Wave 1, lane WG2: behaviour runner replay and restore\n90: - [x] T010 [P] Run no code from an untrusted backfill checkout (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('runs nothing from a checkout that is neither the project root nor a marked arena')`: make a temporary folder holding a fake `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` and a fake `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, each writing its own marker file into that folder when run, write a one-line log whose `locator.projectDir` names the folder, call `backfillRunLog` with `promptFor: () => 'prompt'`, `brief: async () => 'unknown'` and the default warm and replay, and expect `ok` true, `lines` 1, `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` on the written line and neither marker file. Add `it('replays a checkout that holds the arena marker')`, where the folder also holds `.git/skilled-behaviour-arena` and stub `warm` and `replay` record their `checkoutDir`, expecting both to record that folder. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the first case fail because both fakes ran. Then in `CO` add `realpathSync` to the `node:fs` import and `export function trustedCheckout(checkoutDir)`, which returns `true` when `realpathSync(checkoutDir)` equals `realpathSync(REPO_ROOT)` or `existsSync(join(checkoutDir, '.git', 'skilled-behaviour-arena'))` holds, and `false` when either call throws, with a comment that a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Give `backfillRunLog` a `trusted = trustedCheckout` option, named in its jsdoc, and before the warm-up, when `checkoutDir !== null && !trusted(checkoutDir)`, set the offer to `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'untrusted_checkout' }` and skip the warm-up and the replay. In the existing case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once`, pass `trusted: () => true`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-backfill-tru... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n91: - [x] T011 [P] Read NUL-separated status in the restore (`WR`, `WRT`). Test first: in `WRT`, add `it('removes a created file whose name holds a space')`, which takes a `statusSnapshot`