r-tool-schemas.ts:310` `` with ``the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``, `` `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634` `` with ``the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` ``, and each of `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` `` and `` `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290` `` with ``the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` ``. Leave the citations of `lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, `tools/advisor-recommend.ts` and `skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts`. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor-tool-schemas\\.ts:[0-9]|handlers/advisor-recommend\\.ts:[0-9]\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendationSchema\" $ARM` prints 3, `rg -c \"AdvisorRecommendInputSchema\" $ARM` prints 2 and `bash $PL/probe-catalog-lines.sh` prints no `advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and no `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` line.\n121: \n122: ### Wave 1, lane WG8: doctor embed and setup contracts\n123: - [x] T031 [P] Give a failed restore its own exit-3 outcome (`DAE`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow reads a failed restore as a partly written tree')`, which takes the one line of `EMBED_YAML` that contains `Exit 3 means` and asserts it matches `/ERROR: the restore failed/`, `/quote both ERROR lines/` and `/takes precedence over the restored: outcome/`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on the first pattern. Then in `DAE`, inside the same quoted string that starts `Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup.`, append `When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0 and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `workflow names the restore failure: 1`.\n124: - [x] T032 [P] Name the backup folder by the plan digest (`DAE`, `RTS`, `DAC`). Test first: in `DAC`, add `test('the embed workflow and route name the backup folder the engine makes')`, asserting that `EMBED_YAML` and `routeFor('embed').gate3_location` each contain `doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/` and not `<timestamp>`, and that the route text contains `temporary directory`. Run `NT $DAC` and see it fail on `<timestamp>`. Then in `DAE` replace `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/` with `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/`, and in `RTS`, inside the embed route's `gate3_location`, replace `taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte` with `taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DAC` reports `fail 0`, `RV` exits 0, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `bash $PL/probe-embed-contract.sh` prints `route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes`.\n125: - [x] T033 [P] Give the setup router the workflow's reason for absent hook health (`DSM`, `DSCT`). Test first: in `DSCT`, inside `test('the setup workflow and router both name the unrecorded hook health state'`, add `assert.match(SETUP_ROUTER, /because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet/)` and `assert.doesNotMatch(SETUP_ROUTER, /SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG/)`. Run `NT $DSCT` and see it fail on the first assertion. Then in `DSM` replace ``When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded and names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, the setting that turns the records on.`` with `When the daemon holds no hook health records, the leg prints hook health not recorded, because no prompt hook has written a record for this checkout yet: OpenCode has no prompt hook that writes one and an unapproved Codex hook never runs.` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 0` and `RV` and `SRM` exit 0.\n126: \n127: ### Wave 1, lane WG9: doctor check scripts\n128: - [x] T034 [P] Read a hook command the way a shell runs it (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: in `HWT`, add one `test` per launch that writes `writeClaudeSettings(f.root, { UserPromptSubmit: [{ hooks: [{ type: 'command', command }] }] })` and expects exit 0 and `ok claude`, for the commands `` `env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `/usr/bin/env node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `bash -lc \"node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``, `` `zsh -c 'node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}'` ``, `` `node --no-warnings ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, `` `cd \"$PWD\"&& node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` `` and `` `cd /tmp; node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}` ``, and one more that expects exit 1 and `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` for `` `echo \"x && node ${CLAUDE_MARKER}\"` ``. Run `NT $HWT` and see the seven launches print `hook-missing` and the `echo` case print `ok`. Then in `HW` replace `stripQuotes`, `startsCommand` and the body of `runsMarker(command, marker)` with a reader that splits the command into words outside quotes, honouring single quotes, double quotes and a backslash escape, and ends a simple command at `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|` or a newline outside quotes, even one stuck to a word. A simple command is wired when, after any leading `NAME=value` words, its first word is `node` or a path ending `/node` and its first word after any words starting `-` ends with the marker. A first word of `env` or a path ending `/env` is dropped with the `NAME=value` and `-` words after it before that test. A first word of `bash`, `sh` or `zsh`, or a path ending in one, followed by a word that starts with a single `-` and holds `c`, makes the word after it a script that is read again as commands, at most two levels deep. A quoted word is otherwise only an argument, so an `echo` of a quoted script stays unwired. Keep the comment saying a mention is not a wired hook. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with every existing case unchanged, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin`, and `n... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n129: - [x] T035 [P] Count only verified copies as expected in A10 (`CHK`, `CHKT`). Test first: in `CHKT`, in the case `A10 leaves a missing pointer out of the count and names it after the copies`, replace the assertion that the detail matches `/^5\\/6 copies as expected/u` with `assert.equal(copies.detail, '3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing', ...)`. Run `NT $CHKT` and see it print `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing`. Then in `CHK`'s `rowRuntimeCopies`, count as expected only the entries whose `state` is `PASS`, count as reported only the `INFO` entries whose `kind` is not `pointer missing`, and build the detail as `<expected>/<total> copies as expected` followed by `, <n> unmeasured`, `, <n> reported only` and `, <n> pointer missing`, each only when its count is above 0. Leave the row's state rule as it is. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `NT $CHKT` reports `fail 0` and `A10Q` prints a detail whose first number equals its `pass` count and whose `reported only` number equals its `reported` count, which reads `3/6 copies as expected, 2 reported only, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` while the manifest holds the six entries it held at planning.\n130: \n131: ### Wave 1, coordinator: the parent phase map\n132: - [x] T036 [C] Correct three rows of the parent phase map (`PS`). Re-read `PS` and the status rows of the 007, 014 and 015 child specs first. In row 7, after `(R8 transcripts, G2, G5)` add `. It stays open until the final behaviour arm, run on fresh arenas after the merge to main by operator instruction of 2026-11-13, settles T020, T046 and the acceptance rows AC-004, AC-005 and AC-007`. Set the Status cell of rows 14 and 15 to `Complete`. Change no other row. Verify: `bash $PL/probe-phase-map.sh | rg -e '^row (7|14|15) ' | rg -c differs` prints nothing and `rg -c \"until the final behaviour arm\" $PS` prints 1.\n133: \n134: ### Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\n135: Two independent verifiers read the wave 1 diff (`$SP/verify-wg1-4.md`, `$SP/verify-wg5-9.md`): 33 of 33 tasks do what their line says, no P0 or P1 and nine P2. The four below were built by the coordinator. Four were left: the g2 run-line write in `R` has no suite test and stays covered by `$PL/probe-arm-fixture.mjs`, which T039 reruns. The literal marker path in `trustedCheckout` agrees with the arena builder and fails toward untrusted. A busy code split across two writes now counts as busy, which is a busy variant. The catalog pages of four other skills that name `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` belong to other skills and the advisor's hook path still carries that field, so they are outside this phase.\n136: - [x] T042 [C] Narrow the no-edit pattern so a change request that limits its scope keeps its command (`CA`, `CAG`). The bare `no changes` alternative read `refactor the parser so there are no changes to its public api` as a no-edit request. Replace it with `make no changes|no changes yet` and add an `it.each` of three scope-limiting change requests expecting `isNoEditRequest` to be `false`. Verify: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `rg -c \"make no changes\\|no changes yet\" $CA` prints 1.\n137: - [x] T043 [C] End the `--row-id` sentence before `--json` (`RA`). Verify: ``rg -c 'usage error with `--runtime`\\. `--json` prints' $RA`` prints 1.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 138]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593440822,"end":1794593441231}}}}
