{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593446623,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","part":{"partID":"prt_1d61ad92d001fYqQGXng1DKL7s","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","messageID":"msg_1d61ac979001tzglm2s95Wx210","type":"tool","id":"call_b7c0e17b728e4dcda4129124","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md","offset":137},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 137-277\n137: - [x] T043 [C] End the `--row-id` sentence before `--json` (`RA`). Verify: ``rg -c 'usage error with `--runtime`\\. `--json` prints' $RA`` prints 1.\n138: - [x] T044 [C] Read the launch shapes the first reader got wrong (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: seven launches a shell runs (`env -u NAME`, `node -r`, a subshell, a brace group, `exec`, a background command first and a backslash line continuation) expecting `ok claude`, and five that run nothing (an unclosed quote, `node --check`, `node -e`, a launch inside a comment and a shell script that takes its own `-c`) expecting `hook-missing`. Nine of the twelve failed before the change. Verify: `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with 28 passed, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and `node $PL/probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints the lines T034 names.\n139: - [x] T045 [C] Make the plugin field test fail on a dropped owner (`PJT`). The row's owner equalled its skill id, so the label did not change when the owner was dropped. Give the row the skill id `system-spec-kit` and keep the owner `sk-doc`. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0`, and a copy of the test with the `ownerSkillId` line removed reports `fail 1`.\n140: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n145: ## Phase 3: Verification\n146: \n147: - [x] T037 [C] Rebuild and run every suite (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, `TC`, `VALL`, `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Verify: the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `$SP/before.txt`, the child-flag run reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n148: - [x] T038 [C] Hold every floor equal (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and `A10Q`, write each beside its `before.txt` line and end the file with `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` only when each `FLOOR` and `EVAL` line does. When one differs, write the difference, mark this task `[B]` and do not tune a pattern to restore it. Verify: each of the four `FLOOR` lines and the `EVAL` line equals its `before.txt` line character for character, and `rg -c \"^RESULT: every floor equals its before line$\" $SP/after.txt` prints 1.\n149: - [x] T039 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the 18 probes in `PL` after the build, as T002 did, and write their output. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> undefined' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> false' -e 'fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2' -e 'arm refused mixed_row_arms' -e 'run line records the fixture: true' -e 'variables left changed: []' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1' -e 'bash -lc: exit 0 ok claude' -e 'echo with a quoted script: exit 1 hook-missing' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 1' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes' -e 'privacy case persists a record: true' -e 'LF: raw break in literal false, parses true' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: true' -e 'compiledRouteSummary lines: []' -e 'stdout= stderr=score-command-transcripts.mjs: --row-id narrows --summary only' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 19.\n150: - [x] T040 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `G diff --quiet BASE -- AGENTS.md` exits 0, `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9]|WG[0-9]|DR[0-9]-P|SA[0-9]-P|iter[0-9]-P)\"` prints nothing, the same `rg` over `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg -c \"^\\+.*/create:(sk-)?skill\\b\"` prints nothing, `G diff --name-only BASE -- .skilled .opencode` together with the untracked files in `G status --short -- .skilled .opencode` names only files that T003 to T035 name, and `G diff BASE -U0 -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md | rg -c '^\\+\\| (7|14|15) \\|'` prints 3.\n151: - [x] T041 [C] Close out (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Write the summary from `$SP/after.txt` and `$SP/repro-after.txt`, mark each acceptance row with the evidence observed, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder <this folder> --apply` and then strict validation. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n157: ## Completion Criteria\n158: \n159: - [x] All tasks marked `[x]`\n160: - [x] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n161: - [x] `$SP/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` and `$SP/repro-after.txt` holds every fixed output T039 names\n162: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n163: \n164: ---\n165: \n166: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n167: ## Cross-References\n168: \n169: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n170: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n171: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n172: - **Review report**: `../review/review-report.md`\n173: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n174: \n175: ---\n176: \n177: ## Verification Checklist\n178: \n179: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n180: ## Verification Protocol\n181: \n182: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n183: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n184: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n185: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n186: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n187: \n188: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A floor that moves blocks the phase.\n189: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n190: \n191: ---\n192: \n193: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n194: ## Pre-Implementation\n195: \n196: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 016 is committed, and the before numbers and the reproductions are in `scratch/` (T001, T002). Evidence: `scratch/before.txt` shows the `log` printing `ec1869dae8`, `test -e` `exit=1` and an empty status, and `scratch/repro-before.txt` holds 18 probes, each `exit=0`, with the T002 count printing 17.\n197: - [x] CHK-002 [P0] Each task line ends with a verify clause: `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9].*Verify: ' tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9]' tasks.md` print the same number. Evidence: both print 45 at close-out.\n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n203: ## Code Quality\n204: \n205: - [x] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on every changed `.mjs`, `.cjs` and `.js` file. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `TC` `exit=0`, and the close-out `node --check` exits 0 on all 15 changed script files.\n206: - [x] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id (T040). Evidence: the close-out rerun of the T040 label scan prints nothing on the diff against `ec1869dae8` and on the new test file.\n207: - [x] CHK-012 [P0] `CA` still has no import, so the scorer can import it without a cycle: `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing. Evidence: the close-out rerun prints nothing and exits 1.\n208: - [x] CHK-013 [P1] The generated blocks in `CA` stay the deriver's own: `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` after T009 and after T032. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` on the final tree, which holds both changes.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n214: ## Testing Checklist\n215: \n216: - [x] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor equals its before line (T038). Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line`, and its four `FLOOR` lines and `[160,50,21,5]` equal `scratch/before.txt`.\n217: - [x] CHK-021 [P0] Each fix's verify recorded its test failing before the change and passing after, except the cases the spec names as passing today. Evidence: the `scratch/logs/` report of each of the 20 test-first tasks (T003 to T005, T008 to T016, T022, T023, T029, T031 to T035) records its red run, T044 records nine of twelve new cases failing first, and T042's three cases match verifier finding F1, whose probe read those prompts as no-edit before the change.\n218: - [x] CHK-022 [P0] The planning probes print the fixed outputs (T039). Evidence: the T039 count on `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints 19, and all 18 probes record `exit=0`.\n219: - [x] CHK-023 [P1] The fallback envelope test passes under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (T037). Evidence: the `child-flag envelope` run in `scratch/after.txt` reads `Tests 4 passed (4)`.\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n221: \n222: ---\n223: \n224: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n225: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n226: \n227: - [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each finding has a class: the no-edit gate `cross-consumer` (attach path, two scorer gates, explainer), the backfill trust and the busy scan `algorithmic`, the quoted restore and the launch reader `class-of-bug` (every quoted path and every wrapper shape), the arm label and the replayed fixture `instance-only`, the two measurement scripts `test-isolation`, and the doc, comment and contract findings `instance-only`. Evidence: the cross-consumer fix reaches all four consumers, `command-attach.ts:335`, `fusion.ts:677` and `:881` and `text.ts:150`, and the restore reads every path through `status --porcelain -z`.\n228: - [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -ln \"without making changes\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists no code file after T004. Evidence: the close-out rerun no longer lists `scorer/text.ts`. Its two code hits are the shared pattern itself in `command-attach.ts` and a `--dry-run` help string in `mcp-code-mode/scripts/install.sh`, which is not a copy of the pattern.\n229: - [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers of every changed symbol are the ones `plan.md` lists, and the consumer `rg` in its required inventories prints no unlisted file. Evidence: the close-out rerun lists `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/text.ts` and `fusion.ts` lines 20, 36, 677, 709, 717, 881 and 1236, `backfillRunLog` only in `command-offer.vitest.ts` and `copies as expected` only in `agents-md-check.cjs` and its test.\n230: - [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The path, parser and trust fixes carry adversarial cases: a file name with a space, a rename to a name with a space, a checkout with fake code and no marker, a marker inside a quoted `echo` argument and a marker named only in a `description` field. Evidence: `worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and `command-offer.vitest.ts` hold the first three, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `names a runtime whose entry echoes a quoted command` and `names a runtime whose entry only describes the script`.\n231: - [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix rows `plan.md` lists for the no-edit gate and the launch reader each exist in the tests T003 to T005 and T034 add. Evidence: the four wordings run on `attachCommand` and on `isReadOnlyExplainer`, the curly wording runs on `commandMeaningEligible`, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `node`, `env`, `/usr/bin/env`, `bash -lc`, `zsh -c`, a flag, a stuck separator and a quoted `echo`. `sh` has no case of its own and shares one list with `bash` and `zsh` at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:241`.\n232: - [x] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The hostile environment variants ran: the cost script with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` in its parent and the capture compared against a snapshot of the caller's environment. Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>` and `variables left changed: []`, and the T014 and T015 cases pass in `VALL`.\n233: - [x] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on: `scratch/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name the base commit with the changes in the working tree. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` reads `base ec1869dae8 with the changes in the working tree`, and the summary's Metadata names `ec1869dae8`.\n234: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n235: \n236: ---\n237: \n238: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n239: ## Security\n240: \n241: - [x] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text or opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls in `scratch/logs/` names `holdout-prompts`, and the coordinator commands in `scratch/before.txt` and `scratch/after.txt` name no holdout file.\n242: - [x] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session, runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls names a model CLI or a home path, and the coordinator records hold no live arm or hook approval.\n243: - [x] CHK-032 [P0] The backfill spawns nothing from an untrusted checkout (T010). Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`.\n244: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n245: \n246: ---\n247: \n248: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n249: ## Documentation\n250: \n251: - [x] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `acceptance-criteria.md` state the same names, floors and fixed outputs. Evidence: `spec.md` REQ-001 now names `make no changes` and `no changes yet`, as T042 built them.\n252: - [x] CHK-041 [P1] The README, playbook, catalog, workflow and router edits match the code (T008, T017 to T024, T030 to T033): each verify prints what it says on the final tree. Evidence: the close-out `rg` reruns of T008, T017 to T021, T024 and T030 print what their lines name, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line, `DALL` reads `fail 0` and `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints the T031 to T033 probe lines.\n253: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n254: \n255: ---\n256: \n257: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n258: ## File Organization\n259: \n260: - [x] CHK-050 [P1] The before and after records and the reproductions live in `scratch/` only, and no temporary probe or test folder remains. Evidence: the records are in `scratch/` only, and the `advisor-status` suite now removes every temporary tree it makes: a run of that file left the count of `advisor-status-*` folders in the system temp folder unchanged.\n261: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n266: ## Verification Summary\n267: \n268: | Category | Total | Verified |\n269: |----------|-------|----------|\n270: | P0 Items | 15 | 15/15 |\n271: | P1 Items | 8 | 8/8 |\n272: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n273: \n274: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n275: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n276: \n277: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 137-277\n137: - [x] T043 [C] End the `--row-id` sentence before `--json` (`RA`). Verify: ``rg -c 'usage error with `--runtime`\\. `--json` prints' $RA`` prints 1.\n138: - [x] T044 [C] Read the launch shapes the first reader got wrong (`HW`, `HWT`). Test first: seven launches a shell runs (`env -u NAME`, `node -r`, a subshell, a brace group, `exec`, a background command first and a backslash line continuation) expecting `ok claude`, and five that run nothing (an unclosed quote, `node --check`, `node -e`, a launch inside a comment and a shell script that takes its own `-c`) expecting `hook-missing`. Nine of the twelve failed before the change. Verify: `NT $HWT` reports `fail 0` with 28 passed, `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and `node $PL/probe-hook-shapes.cjs` prints the lines T034 names.\n139: - [x] T045 [C] Make the plugin field test fail on a dropped owner (`PJT`). The row's owner equalled its skill id, so the label did not change when the owner was dropped. Give the row the skill id `system-spec-kit` and keep the owner `sk-doc`. Verify: `VP` reports `fail 0`, and a copy of the test with the `ownerSkillId` line removed reports `fail 1`.\n140: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n145: ## Phase 3: Verification\n146: \n147: - [x] T037 [C] Rebuild and run every suite (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, `TC`, `VALL`, `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Verify: the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `$SP/before.txt`, the child-flag run reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `PBV` prints its `PASS` line.\n148: - [x] T038 [C] Hold every floor equal (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL` and `A10Q`, write each beside its `before.txt` line and end the file with `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` only when each `FLOOR` and `EVAL` line does. When one differs, write the difference, mark this task `[B]` and do not tune a pattern to restore it. Verify: each of the four `FLOOR` lines and the `EVAL` line equals its `before.txt` line character for character, and `rg -c \"^RESULT: every floor equals its before line$\" $SP/after.txt` prints 1.\n149: - [x] T039 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the 18 probes in `PL` after the build, as T002 did, and write their output. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> undefined' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> false' -e 'fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md false, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm g2' -e 'arm refused mixed_row_arms' -e 'run line records the fixture: true' -e 'variables left changed: []' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED, retriesAttempted 1' -e 'bash -lc: exit 0 ok claude' -e 'echo with a quoted script: exit 1 hook-missing' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 1' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: yes' -e 'privacy case persists a record: true' -e 'LF: raw break in literal false, parses true' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: true' -e 'compiledRouteSummary lines: []' -e 'stdout= stderr=score-command-transcripts.mjs: --row-id narrows --summary only' $SP/repro-after.txt` prints 19.\n150: - [x] T040 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `G diff --quiet BASE -- AGENTS.md` exits 0, `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9]|WG[0-9]|DR[0-9]-P|SA[0-9]-P|iter[0-9]-P)\"` prints nothing, the same `rg` over `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` prints nothing, `G diff BASE -U0 -- .skilled .opencode | rg -c \"^\\+.*/create:(sk-)?skill\\b\"` prints nothing, `G diff --name-only BASE -- .skilled .opencode` together with the untracked files in `G status --short -- .skilled .opencode` names only files that T003 to T035 name, and `G diff BASE -U0 -- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md | rg -c '^\\+\\| (7|14|15) \\|'` prints 3.\n151: - [x] T041 [C] Close out (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Write the summary from `$SP/after.txt` and `$SP/repro-after.txt`, mark each acceptance row with the evidence observed, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder <this folder> --apply` and then strict validation. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n157: ## Completion Criteria\n158: \n159: - [x] All tasks marked `[x]`\n160: - [x] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n161: - [x] `$SP/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line` and `$SP/repro-after.txt` holds every fixed output T039 names\n162: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n163: \n164: ---\n165: \n166: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n167: ## Cross-References\n168: \n169: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n170: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n171: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n172: - **Review report**: `../review/review-report.md`\n173: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n174: \n175: ---\n176: \n177: ## Verification Checklist\n178: \n179: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n180: ## Verification Protocol\n181: \n182: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n183: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n184: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n185: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n186: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n187: \n188: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A floor that moves blocks the phase.\n189: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n190: \n191: ---\n192: \n193: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n194: ## Pre-Implementation\n195: \n196: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 016 is committed, and the before numbers and the reproductions are in `scratch/` (T001, T002). Evidence: `scratch/before.txt` shows the `log` printing `ec1869dae8`, `test -e` `exit=1` and an empty status, and `scratch/repro-before.txt` holds 18 probes, each `exit=0`, with the T002 count printing 17.\n197: - [x] CHK-002 [P0] Each task line ends with a verify clause: `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9].*Verify: ' tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9]' tasks.md` print the same number. Evidence: both print 45 at close-out.\n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n203: ## Code Quality\n204: \n205: - [x] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on every changed `.mjs`, `.cjs` and `.js` file. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `TC` `exit=0`, and the close-out `node --check` exits 0 on all 15 changed script files.\n206: - [x] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id (T040). Evidence: the close-out rerun of the T040 label scan prints nothing on the diff against `ec1869dae8` and on the new test file.\n207: - [x] CHK-012 [P0] `CA` still has no import, so the scorer can import it without a cycle: `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing. Evidence: the close-out rerun prints nothing and exits 1.\n208: - [x] CHK-013 [P1] The generated blocks in `CA` stay the deriver's own: `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` after T009 and after T032. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` on the final tree, which holds both changes.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n214: ## Testing Checklist\n215: \n216: - [x] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor equals its before line (T038). Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` ends `RESULT: every floor equals its before line`, and its four `FLOOR` lines and `[160,50,21,5]` equal `scratch/before.txt`.\n217: - [x] CHK-021 [P0] Each fix's verify recorded its test failing before the change and passing after, except the cases the spec names as passing today. Evidence: the `scratch/logs/` report of each of the 20 test-first tasks (T003 to T005, T008 to T016, T022, T023, T029, T031 to T035) records its red run, T044 records nine of twelve new cases failing first, and T042's three cases match verifier finding F1, whose probe read those prompts as no-edit before the change.\n218: - [x] CHK-022 [P0] The planning probes print the fixed outputs (T039). Evidence: the T039 count on `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints 19, and all 18 probes record `exit=0`.\n219: - [x] CHK-023 [P1] The fallback envelope test passes under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (T037). Evidence: the `child-flag envelope` run in `scratch/after.txt` reads `Tests 4 passed (4)`.\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n221: \n222: ---\n223: \n224: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n225: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n226: \n227: - [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each finding has a class: the no-edit gate `cross-consumer` (attach path, two scorer gates, explainer), the backfill trust and the busy scan `algorithmic`, the quoted restore and the launch reader `class-of-bug` (every quoted path and every wrapper shape), the arm label and the replayed fixture `instance-only`, the two measurement scripts `test-isolation`, and the doc, comment and contract findings `instance-only`. Evidence: the cross-consumer fix reaches all four consumers, `command-attach.ts:335`, `fusion.ts:677` and `:881` and `text.ts:150`, and the restore reads every path through `status --porcelain -z`.\n228: - [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -ln \"without making changes\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists no code file after T004. Evidence: the close-out rerun no longer lists `scorer/text.ts`. Its two code hits are the shared pattern itself in `command-attach.ts` and a `--dry-run` help string in `mcp-code-mode/scripts/install.sh`, which is not a copy of the pattern.\n229: - [x] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers of every changed symbol are the ones `plan.md` lists, and the consumer `rg` in its required inventories prints no unlisted file. Evidence: the close-out rerun lists `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/text.ts` and `fusion.ts` lines 20, 36, 677, 709, 717, 881 and 1236, `backfillRunLog` only in `command-offer.vitest.ts` and `copies as expected` only in `agents-md-check.cjs` and its test.\n230: - [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The path, parser and trust fixes carry adversarial cases: a file name with a space, a rename to a name with a space, a checkout with fake code and no marker, a marker inside a quoted `echo` argument and a marker named only in a `description` field. Evidence: `worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and `command-offer.vitest.ts` hold the first three, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `names a runtime whose entry echoes a quoted command` and `names a runtime whose entry only describes the script`.\n231: - [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix rows `plan.md` lists for the no-edit gate and the launch reader each exist in the tests T003 to T005 and T034 add. Evidence: the four wordings run on `attachCommand` and on `isReadOnlyExplainer`, the curly wording runs on `commandMeaningEligible`, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `node`, `env`, `/usr/bin/env`, `bash -lc`, `zsh -c`, a flag, a stuck separator and a quoted `echo`. `sh` has no case of its own and shares one list with `bash` and `zsh` at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:241`.\n232: - [x] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The hostile environment variants ran: the cost script with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` in its parent and the capture compared against a snapshot of the caller's environment. Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=<unset>` and `variables left changed: []`, and the T014 and T015 cases pass in `VALL`.\n233: - [x] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on: `scratch/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name the base commit with the changes in the working tree. Evidence: `scratch/after.txt` reads `base ec1869dae8 with the changes in the working tree`, and the summary's Metadata names `ec1869dae8`.\n234: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n235: \n236: ---\n237: \n238: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n239: ## Security\n240: \n241: - [x] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text or opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls in `scratch/logs/` names `holdout-prompts`, and the coordinator commands in `scratch/before.txt` and `scratch/after.txt` name no holdout file.\n242: - [x] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session, runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. Evidence: none of the 673 worker tool calls names a model CLI or a home path, and the coordinator records hold no live arm or hook approval.\n243: - [x] CHK-032 [P0] The backfill spawns nothing from an untrusted checkout (T010). Evidence: `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false`.\n244: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n245: \n246: ---\n247: \n248: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n249: ## Documentation\n250: \n251: - [x] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `acceptance-criteria.md` state the same names, floors and fixed outputs. Evidence: `spec.md` REQ-001 now names `make no changes` and `no changes yet`, as T042 built them.\n252: - [x] CHK-041 [P1] The README, playbook, catalog, workflow and router edits match the code (T008, T017 to T024, T030 to T033): each verify prints what it says on the final tree. Evidence: the close-out `rg` reruns of T008, T017 to T021, T024 and T030 print what their lines name, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line, `DALL` reads `fail 0` and `scratch/repro-after.txt` prints the T031 to T033 probe lines.\n253: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n254: \n255: ---\n256: \n257: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n258: ## File Organization\n259: \n260: - [x] CHK-050 [P1] The before and after records and the reproductions live in `scratch/` only, and no temporary probe or test folder remains. Evidence: the records are in `scratch/` only, and the `advisor-status` suite now removes every temporary tree it makes: a run of that file left the count of `advisor-status-*` folders in the system temp folder unchanged.\n261: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n266: ## Verification Summary\n267: \n268: | Category | Total | Verified |\n269: |----------|-------|----------|\n270: | P0 Items | 15 | 15/15 |\n271: | P1 Items | 8 | 8/8 |\n272: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n273: \n274: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n275: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n276: \n277: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md\",\"offset\":137}"},"time":{"start":1794593446189,"end":1794593446623}}}}
