{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593686655,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","part":{"partID":"prt_1d61e3a12001H1jNWwy7K7e6BA","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","messageID":"msg_1d61e2aab001tE2ynVBb1uF5ef","type":"tool","id":"call_3e94f6604ac74929ba61c4b8","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Operator review focus: narrow pass three over the `advisor-runtime` area; this iteration read the changed lines of the shared no-edit gate and of the subprocess busy scan, then followed each changed function to its callers. The focus's \"changed lines and callers\" boundary is what selected the four files below.\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 calls)\n- Base/HEAD: `ec1869dae8..1ca14a44988d3812ef18d968aba304ed31481648`\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n`@deep-review` LEAF iteration dispatched by the fan-out lineage `advisor-runtime-3`, session `fanout-advisor-runtime-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`. Sources read this iteration: `review-scope-3.txt`, `017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md`, `git diff ec1869dae8..HEAD` for the four files below, the current code at the cited lines, and `review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/steer.md` (absent at read, so no lead ruling applied).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:286-339`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:2-6,147-163`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:17-20,674-690,876-887`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:90-95,214-300,352-372`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:25-75,123-140`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts:26-40`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:334-347`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts:42-91`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:470-476` (caller of `attachCommand`)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **`make no changes` reads a scope-limiting change request as a no-edit request** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- The widened pattern adds the alternative `make no changes` without a boundary that keeps it from matching a constraint inside a change request. `isNoEditRequest('create an agent that refactors the parser internals and make no changes to its public api')` returns `true`, so `attachCommand` returns `undefined` and the reader who asked for the change gets no command. The same value reaches `isReadOnlyExplainer` (`lib/scorer/text.ts:150`) and both `commandMeaningEligible` gates (`lib/scorer/fusion.ts:677,881`). The task that narrowed the pattern, T042, states the goal \"a change request that limits its scope keeps its command\" and tests `no changes to its public api`; the `make no changes` alternative reintroduces the same class the task removed.\n   Finding class: class-of-bug (the wording class the same pattern introduced, not a single prompt).\n   Scope proof: the alternative is on the changed line `command-attach.ts:289`; its consumers are `text.ts:150`, `fusion.ts:677` and `fusion.ts:881`, all changed in this diff to call the shared helper.\n   Affected surface hints: hub command attachment (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:474`), read-only explainer gate, command-meaning eligibility.\n   Case: `create an agent that refactors the parser internals and make no changes to its public api` returns `undefined` from `attachCommand('sk-doc', {action:'route',selectionKind:'single',targets:[{workflowMode:'sk-create-agent'}]}, prompt)` where `/create:agent` is expected. Verified by a tsx probe of the current source; the three T042 cases still return `false`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | T003/T004/T005 and T042 name the shared helper and its consumers; the consumers call `isNoEditRequest` at the three sites the task names. T042's stated intent is only partly met (finding AR3-P2-001). |\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reported `3 passed (3)`, `56 passed (56)`, exit 0. |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent file in this area. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | Catalog files are in the `doctor-docs` area. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `attachCommand` has one production caller, `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:474`, which passes the raw prompt; the changed gate therefore governs every recommendation that carries a compiled single-mode route.\n- `isReadOnlyExplainer` is the scorer's explainer gate; `readOnlyRouteAllowed` and `commandMeaningEligible` in `fusion.ts` are the two command-eligibility gates the task names (`rg` shows exactly two `isNoEditRequest(promptLower)` call sites in `fusion.ts`).\n- `runAdvisorSubprocess` retry decision reads `attemptResult.sawBusy || SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr)` at `subprocess.ts:371`; `sawBusy` is set on every resolve path in `runSpawnAttempt`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` itself remains exported and is still tested directly (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:49`), so a caller that bypasses `isNoEditRequest` does not get the curly-apostrophe fold. No production caller does; recorded as a design edge, not a finding.\n- The busy scan keeps only the last 64 characters between chunks. `SQLITE_BUSY` and `database is locked` are shorter than 64, and the new split test proves a two-write split after the cap; a marker split with more than 64 characters of unrelated text between its halves is not in reach for SQLite's own message.\n- `subprocess.ts` retry now scans stderr before `capOutput`; a busy marker written after the cap changes a former `NON_ZERO_EXIT` into `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` with one retry, which is the behavior T029 asks for.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `command-attach.ts` still has no `import` statement, so `text.ts` importing it introduces no cycle (checked with `grep '^import' command-attach.ts`, no output).\n- `SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN` has no `g` flag (`subprocess.ts:106`), so repeated `.test` calls are stateless.\n- The T003, T004 and T005 matrix cases pass: the four no-edit endings, the curly-apostrophe helper case and the change-request cases all hold in the run above.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A circular-import defect from `text.ts` importing `command-attach.js`: ruled out because `command-attach.ts` imports nothing.\n- A lost-retry defect from the new `sawBusy` flag: ruled out by reading every `resolve` in `runSpawnAttempt` and the retry condition; both paths carry the flag.\n- A wrongly-failing `attachCommand` on the T042 scope-limiting cases: ruled out by running the three test files; the three cases pass. Only the `make no changes` variant fails.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the routing-accuracy scripts `command-offer.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, plus `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `derive-command-bridges.cjs`\n- Reason: the library and gate changes are now covered; the remaining changed production files are the runners and the bridge generator.\n- Rotation status: correctness remains current until the runner pass completes.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none blocked; direct-read plus diff reading is productive for this narrow pass.\n- Required evidence: per-file diff, current code, caller reads, one concrete input per finding.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Operator review focus: narrow pass three over the `advisor-runtime` area; this iteration read the changed lines of the shared no-edit gate and of the subprocess busy scan, then followed each changed function to its callers. The focus's \\\"changed lines and callers\\\" boundary is what selected the four files below.\\n- Budget profile: verify (11-13 calls)\\n- Base/HEAD: `ec1869dae8..1ca14a44988d3812ef18d968aba304ed31481648`\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n`@deep-review` LEAF iteration dispatched by the fan-out lineage `advisor-runtime-3`, session `fanout-advisor-runtime-3-1794593402980-zhrui5`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`. Sources read this iteration: `review-scope-3.txt`, `017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md`, `git diff ec1869dae8..HEAD` for the four files below, the current code at the cited lines, and `review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/steer.md` (absent at read, so no lead ruling applied).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:286-339`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:2-6,147-163`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:17-20,674-690,876-887`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:90-95,214-300,352-372`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:25-75,123-140`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts:26-40`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:334-347`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts:42-91`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:470-476` (caller of `attachCommand`)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **`make no changes` reads a scope-limiting change request as a no-edit request** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289` -- The widened pattern adds the alternative `make no changes` without a boundary that keeps it from matching a constraint inside a change request. `isNoEditRequest('create an agent that refactors the parser internals and make no changes to its public api')` returns `true`, so `attachCommand` returns `undefined` and the reader who asked for the change gets no command. The same value reaches `isReadOnlyExplainer` (`lib/scorer/text.ts:150`) and both `commandMeaningEligible` gates (`lib/scorer/fusion.ts:677,881`). The task that narrowed the pattern, T042, states the goal \\\"a change request that limits its scope keeps its command\\\" and tests `no changes to its public api`; the `make no changes` alternative reintroduces the same class the task removed.\\n   Finding class: class-of-bug (the wording class the same pattern introduced, not a single prompt).\\n   Scope proof: the alternative is on the changed line `command-attach.ts:289`; its consumers are `text.ts:150`, `fusion.ts:677` and `fusion.ts:881`, all changed in this diff to call the shared helper.\\n   Affected surface hints: hub command attachment (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:474`), read-only explainer gate, command-meaning eligibility.\\n   Case: `create an agent that refactors the parser internals and make no changes to its public api` returns `undefined` from `attachCommand('sk-doc', {action:'route',selectionKind:'single',targets:[{workflowMode:'sk-create-agent'}]}, prompt)` where `/create:agent` is expected. Verified by a tsx probe of the current source; the three T042 cases still return `false`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | T003/T004/T005 and T042 name the shared helper and its consumers; the consumers call `isNoEditRequest` at the three sites the task names. T042's stated intent is only partly met (finding AR3-P2-001). |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reported `3 passed (3)`, `56 passed (56)`, exit 0. |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | No agent file in this area. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | Catalog files are in the `doctor-docs` area. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `attachCommand` has one production caller, `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:474`, which passes the raw prompt; the changed gate therefore governs every recommendation that carries a compiled single-mode route.\\n- `isReadOnlyExplainer` is the scorer's explainer gate; `readOnlyRouteAllowed` and `commandMeaningEligible` in `fusion.ts` are the two command-eligibility gates the task names (`rg` shows exactly two `isNoEditRequest(promptLower)` call sites in `fusion.ts`).\\n- `runAdvisorSubprocess` retry decision reads `attemptResult.sawBusy || SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN.test(attemptResult.stderr)` at `subprocess.ts:371`; `sawBusy` is set on every resolve path in `runSpawnAttempt`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` itself remains exported and is still tested directly (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:49`), so a caller that bypasses `isNoEditRequest` does not get the curly-apostrophe fold. No production caller does; recorded as a design edge, not a finding.\\n- The busy scan keeps only the last 64 characters between chunks. `SQLITE_BUSY` and `database is locked` are shorter than 64, and the new split test proves a two-write split after the cap; a marker split with more than 64 characters of unrelated text between its halves is not in reach for SQLite's own message.\\n- `subprocess.ts` retry now scans stderr before `capOutput`; a busy marker written after the cap changes a former `NON_ZERO_EXIT` into `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` with one retry, which is the behavior T029 asks for.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `command-attach.ts` still has no `import` statement, so `text.ts` importing it introduces no cycle (checked with `grep '^import' command-attach.ts`, no output).\\n- `SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN` has no `g` flag (`subprocess.ts:106`), so repeated `.test` calls are stateless.\\n- The T003, T004 and T005 matrix cases pass: the four no-edit endings, the curly-apostrophe helper case and the change-request cases all hold in the run above.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A circular-import defect from `text.ts` importing `command-attach.js`: ruled out because `command-attach.ts` imports nothing.\\n- A lost-retry defect from the new `sawBusy` flag: ruled out by reading every `resolve` in `runSpawnAttempt` and the retry condition; both paths carry the flag.\\n- A wrongly-failing `attachCommand` on the T042 scope-limiting cases: ruled out by running the three test files; the three cases pass. Only the `make no changes` variant fails.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: the routing-accuracy scripts `command-offer.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, plus `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `derive-command-bridges.cjs`\\n- Reason: the library and gate changes are now covered; the remaining changed production files are the runners and the bridge generator.\\n- Rotation status: correctness remains current until the runner pass completes.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none blocked; direct-read plus diff reading is productive for this narrow pass.\\n- Required evidence: per-file diff, current code, caller reads, one concrete input per finding.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794593667602,"end":1794593686655}}}}
