{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794593764204,"sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","part":{"partID":"prt_1d61fb222001YedvjBFVeRtTPt","sessionID":"ses_e29e5c0baffeXQQt48JD3haI5K","messageID":"msg_1d61faacc001KulsP3EKkL230O","type":"tool","id":"call_39b0ebc1a2154c63903c1f7e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-189\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: ### Purpose\n6: \n7: Persistent review state for the advisor-runtime-3 fan-out lineage. Narrow pass three: review only the changed lines of the files whose area in `review-scope-3.txt` is `advisor-runtime`, plus their callers, and report only defects with a concrete input.\n8: \n9: ### Review Charter\n10: \n11: - Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec folder), narrow changed-lines pass over the two remediation commits `ec1869dae8..1ca14a44`.\n12: - Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability, one focus per iteration.\n13: - Stop conditions: convergence (weighted new-finding ratio under 0.10 after the second iteration) or `maxIterations=4`.\n14: - Success criteria: every changed line and its callers read; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete failing input; holdout hygiene proved by a numstat-only check of the sealed file.\n15: - Write surface: this lineage directory only. No code changes, no repo tooling that writes outside it.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. TOPIC\n20: \n21: Command surfacing, review pass three, advisor-runtime area: the shared no-edit gate (`command-attach.ts`, `scorer/text.ts`, `scorer/fusion.ts`), the subprocess busy scan, the routing-accuracy runners (`command-offer.mjs`, `worktree-restore.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`), `measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, the OpenCode plugin and the tests the remediation commits changed.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n26: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n27: - [ ] security\n28: - [ ] traceability\n29: - [ ] maintainability\n30: \n31: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n32: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n33: \n34: - Re-reporting a pass-one or pass-two finding whose fix holds.\n35: - Re-reporting the four items listed under `Verifier follow-ups, coordinator` in `017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md`.\n36: - Duplicating the `doctor-docs` area files (another lineage owns them).\n37: - Reading holdout prompt text. Only counts and a numstat line are permitted.\n38: - Changing code, running builds, the full suite, a daemon or a model CLI.\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n43: \n44: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` under 0.10 at iteration 3 or later with all dimensions covered.\n45: - `maxIterations=4` reached.\n46: - A hard gate failure in the append gateway (exit 2) or a containment breach. Both halt the lineage.\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n51: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n52: - [x] correctness\n53: \n54: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n55: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n56: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n57: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n58: - P1 (Required): 0\n59: - P2 (Suggestions): 1\n60: - Resolved: 0\n61: \n62: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n63: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n64: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n65: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n70: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n71: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n72: \n73: ---\n74: \n75: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n76: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPR